omething a little deeper like there's gonna need to be for spotlight note support, but this is better than falling back to nothing at all.\n\n* Remove underscores from light manager\n\nNeed to set up my venue all over again to actually test this because OOPS but it should be fine, it's compiling without complaints\n\n* Ensure neon manager actually starts\n\nWhy did Awake() work before but not now? Oh well.\n\n* Un-reverse back/center lightstates given to neon lights\n\nI've been wondering about that one for days now, how did I miss that I actually just put the wrong names in the wrong spot, whoops\n\n* Add keyframe response to default cues + blackout/flare tweaks pt 1\n\n* Add keyframe response to default cues + blackout/flare tweaks pt 2\n\nI'm really done this time it's just a few final things that were bugging me enough to come back one last time, anything more I'd want to implement goes deeper than these scripts like specifying spotlights on each band member to respond to a chart's spotlight notes\n\n* ACTUALLY Final change - differentiating all cues pt 1\n\nApparently I was wrong because I thought of one more thing I could still add, the only cue I can't really make much of a difference to is sweep because that requires actual animation on the venue's side.\n\n* whoops that was the wrong file to overwrite first\n\n* ACTUALLY Final change - differentiating all cues pt 2\n\n* Really final change for real this time I swear pt 1\n\nI had just realized a way to implement transitions between, MOST colors at least, when null colors are involved I couldn't figure out a way to make it transition, but for the most part now the lights change more smoothly like they would in commercial games.\n\n* Really final change for real this time I swear pt 2\n\n* Adjustment to transition speed\n\nI forgot to make sure it was even visible at 30 fps first- surprisingly it still keeps up with rapid changes\n\n* Readjust blackout/flare to match\n\n* Fix BlackOutSpot leaving unintended lights on\n\nThis cue just does not ever get used so it really took me this long to realize- whoops.\n\n* Change neon manager to switch over if-else, swap class to struct\n\nWorked out just fine, good to know- there's a decently big difference between this version and the one compatible with the spotlights though, lemme know whenever you want that one\n\n* Remove reference to spotlights (whoops)"
